.UNINDENT
.SS GUI extension
.sp
The GUI configuration plugin extends the configuration of
graphical user interfaces to various options to adjust the look
and feel.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBgroups.*\fP
\fIConfigures the target messaging groups for various object types.\fP
\fIThese parameters should only be touched if you know what you\fP
\fIare doing.\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B groups.pick
Default: \fBPICK\fP
.sp
Type: \fIstring\fP
.sp
Defines the target messaging group for manual picks, e.g.
made in scolv.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B groups.amplitude
Default: \fBAMPLITUDE\fP
.sp
Type: \fIstring\fP
.sp
Defines the target messaging group for amplitudes, e.g.
computed in scolv.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B groups.magnitude
Default: \fBMAGNITUDE\fP
.sp
Type: \fIstring\fP
.sp
Defines the target messaging group for magnitudes. scolv does
not use this group but sends magnitudes together with the
origin to the origin group.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B groups.location
Default: \fBLOCATION\fP
.sp
Type: \fIstring\fP
.sp
Defines the target messaging group for origins created in
e.g. scolv.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B groups.focalMechanism
Default: \fBFOCMECH\fP
.sp
Type: \fIstring\fP
.sp
Defines the target messaging group for focal mechanisms created in
e.g. scolv.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B groups.event
Default: \fBEVENT\fP
.sp
Type: \fIstring\fP
.sp
Defines the target messaging group for events and event
journal entries.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B map.location
Default: \fB@DATADIR@/maps/world%s.png\fP
.sp
Type: \fIstring\fP
.sp
The location and the structure of the map tiles to be used.
This path is composed of zero or more directives and must
include at least one conversion specification. The
specification starts with the \(aq%\(aq and is followed by a
conversion specifier.  Valid specifiers are
.sp
s: to be replaced by tile ID
.sp
l: tile level
.sp
c: tile column
.sp
r: tile row.
.sp
Example for using the OpenStreetMap file structure:
/path/to/maps/%l/%c/%r.png.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B map.format
Default: \fBrectangular\fP
.sp
Type: \fIstring\fP
.sp
Values: \fBrectangular,mercator\fP
.sp
Projection of the map tiles configured in \(dqmap.location\(dq.
.sp
Note: Additional projections may be available by plugins.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B map.cacheSize
Default: \fB0\fP
.sp
Type: \fIint\fP
.sp
Unit: \fIbytes\fP
.sp
Cache size of the map tiles. If 0 is specified. a default
cache size of 32 MBytes is used. The higher the cache size
the better the performance in higher resolutions. A
higher cache size causes less image loader calls but
requires more client memory.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B map.type
Type: \fIstring\fP
.sp
The tile store implementation for considering maps if a
non\-default tile store is configured in \(aqmap.location\(aq.
.sp
The built\-in \(aqxyz\(aq store fetches tiles from any standard
XYZ / slippy\-map server (OpenStreetMap, OpenTopoMap, ESRI,
CartoDB, custom servers); see the \(aqxyz\(aq group below.
Additional stores may be provided by plugins.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B map.customLayers
Type: \fIlist:string\fP
.sp
Allows to add custom layers that are included via plugins.
This is a list of layer names. A plugin must implement
the layer interface and register itself with the
name used in this list. The order of layers is the
default order. The custom layers are prepended to
the maps defaults layers such as the grid and the cities.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B map.layers
Type: \fIstring\fP
.sp
Defines the order of all configured layers. This
includes the standard layers (grid, cities) as
well as custom layers. The name of the grid layer
is \(dqgrid\(dq and the name of the cities
layer is \(dqcities\(dq.
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBmap.xyz.*\fP
\fIConfiguration of the built\-in XYZ tile store\fP
\fI(map.type = xyz). The tile URL template in \(aqmap.location\(aq\fP
\fIuses the tokens {z} (zoom), {x} (column), {y} (row) and\fP
\fI{s} (subdomain), e.g.\fP
\fIhttps://{s}.tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png.\fP
\fINote: some servers (e.g. ESRI) expect {z}/{y}/{x} order.\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B map.xyz.sources
Type: \fIlist:string\fP
.sp
Optional list of tile sources, each serving a contiguous
zoom\-level band, to show different basemaps at different
zoom levels. Each entry has the form
\(dqminLevel:maxLevel:urlTemplate\(dq; only the first two
colons are separators, so the \(dqhttps://\(dq in the URL is
preserved. When set, this overrides \(aqmap.location\(aq. When
empty, \(aqmap.location\(aq is used with minLevel/maxLevel.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B map.xyz.minLevel
Default: \fB0\fP
.sp
Type: \fIuint\fP
.sp
Range: \fB0..29\fP
.sp
Minimum zoom level requested from the single\-source
\(aqmap.location\(aq. Ignored when \(aqmap.xyz.sources\(aq is set.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B map.xyz.maxLevel
Default: \fB19\fP
.sp
Type: \fIuint\fP
.sp
Range: \fB0..29\fP
.sp
Maximum zoom level requested from the single\-source
\(aqmap.location\(aq. Ignored when \(aqmap.xyz.sources\(aq is set.
Provider maxima differ (OSM 19, Google ~21\-22, ESRI 23);
the hard ceiling is 29.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B map.xyz.subdomains
Default: \fBa,b,c\fP
.sp
Type: \fIstring\fP
.sp
Comma\-separated subdomains substituted for {s} in the URL
template, rotated for basic load\-balancing. Leave empty
if the server has no subdomain variants.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B map.xyz.tileSize
Default: \fB256\fP
.sp
Type: \fIstring\fP
.sp
Unit: \fIpx\fP
.sp
Values: \fB256,512\fP
.sp
Edge length of square tiles in pixels. Must match what
the server actually serves; a mismatch renders blurry.
256 = standard tiles, 512 = HiDPI/retina tiles.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B map.xyz.cacheDir
Type: \fIdirectory\fP
.sp
Directory for caching downloaded tiles
(cacheDir/{z}/{x}/{y}). Leave empty to disable disk
caching.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B map.xyz.cacheDuration
Default: \fB86400\fP
.sp
Type: \fIint\fP
.sp
Unit: \fIs\fP
.sp
How long a cached tile is considered fresh before it is
fetched again. \-1 = never expire, 0 = disable caching.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B map.xyz.missingTTL
Default: \fB300\fP
.sp
Type: \fIint\fP
.sp
Unit: \fIs\fP
.sp
How long to remember that a tile returned an HTTP error
(e.g. 404 above a server\(aqs max zoom) before retrying it,
to avoid re\-requesting absent tiles on every redraw.
\-1 = remember for the whole session, 0 = always retry.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B map.xyz.userAgent
Default: \fBSeisComP\-xyztiles/1.0\fP
.sp
Type: \fIstring\fP
.sp
HTTP User\-Agent header sent with every tile request. Set
this to identify your institution when deploying
publicly; required by OSM\(aqs tile usage policy.
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBmap.mercator.*\fP
\fIParameters specifically related to maps loaded with\fP
\fImercator projection.\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B map.mercator.discrete
Default: \fBfalse\fP
.sp
Type: \fIboolean\fP
.sp
Only support discrete zoom levels. The parameter impacts
the effect of \(dqmap.zoom.sensitivity\(dq.
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBmap.layers.events.*\fP
\fIConfiguration options for the events layer that\fP
\fIshows all events on the map that are loaded in the\fP
\fIevent list.\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B map.layers.events.visible
Default: \fBfalse\fP
.sp
Type: \fIboolean\fP
.sp
Show the events layer on maps. Currently only supported
by scolv.
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBmap.layers.fep.*\fP
\fIConfiguration for the fep layer showing the polygons\fP
\fIof FEP (Flinn\-Engdahl\-Polygon) files on maps if they\fP
\fIexist in @DATADIR@/fep or @CONFIGDIR@/fep.\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B map.layers.fep.visible
Default: \fBtrue\fP
.sp
Type: \fIboolean\fP
.sp
Show the fep layer on maps.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B map.layers.cities.topPopulatedPlaces
Default: \fB\-1\fP
.sp
Type: \fIint\fP
.sp
Maximum number of cities to be rendered. If
\(dqscheme.map.cityPopulationWeight\(dq is less
or equal than 0 then all cities are rendered ordered
by population count, highest first.
To show the N most populated places in the visible
map region, set
\(dqscheme.map.cityPopulationWeight\(dq to 0
and set this parameter to N.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B map.zoom.sensitivity
Default: \fB0.5\fP
.sp
Type: \fIdouble\fP
.sp
Zoom sensitivity of the map
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBscheme.*\fP
\fIThis group defines various options controlling the look and feel\fP
\fIof graphical modules. The options include symbols, units,\fP
\fIprecision, color, pen, brush, font, etc. There are various\fP
\fIconventions to define colors, fonts and gradients.\fP
**
\fIColors are defined in HTML\fP
\fIconvention, e.g. as rgb values, hexadecimal numbers or color\fP
\fIkeyword names defined by W3C. If rgb or rgba is used, it must\fP
\fIbe quoted because the comma is handled as list separator by\fP
\fIthe configuration.\fP
\fIExamples: \(dqrgb(0,128,0)\(dq, 00800040, green.\fP
**
\fIGradients are configured as lists of tuples where each tuple\fP
\fIis colon separated in the form value:color. Value is either\fP
\fIint or double and color is again a color definition.\fP
\fIExample: 0:yellow,10:red\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B scheme.showMenu
Default: \fBtrue\fP
.sp
Type: \fIboolean\fP
.sp
Show menu bar.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B scheme.showStatusBar
Default: \fBtrue\fP
.sp
Type: \fIboolean\fP
.sp
Show status bar.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B scheme.tabPosition
Type: \fIstring\fP
.sp
Values: \fBoff,north,south,east,west\fP
.sp
The position of tab bar of GUI applications like scolv.
An unset value lets the application decide where to place
the tab bar. This option might not be supported by all
applications. Valid positions are: off, north, south,
east, west.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B scheme.distanceHypocentral
Default: \fBfalse\fP
.sp
Type: \fIboolean\fP
.sp
Show hypocentral instead of epicentral distances.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B scheme.map.stationSize
Default: \fB8\fP
.sp
Type: \fIint\fP
.sp
Unit: \fIpx\fP
.sp
The station symbol size, e.g., in scmv.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B scheme.map.originSymbolMinSize
Default: \fB9\fP
.sp
Type: \fIint\fP
.sp
Unit: \fIpx\fP
.sp
The minimum symbol size of origins. The size is scaled
with magnitude according to
\(dqscheme.mag.originSymbolScaleMag\(dq.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B scheme.map.originSymbolMinMag
Default: \fB1.2\fP
.sp
Type: \fIdouble\fP
.sp
The minimum magnitude to be represented by an origin
symbol. The symbol size of origins with this or lower
magnitude is configured by
\(dqscheme.mag.originSymbolMinSize\(dq. For origins
with larger magnitudes the symbol sizes are scaled according
to \(dqscheme.mag.originSymbolScaleMag\(dq.
.sp
Starting from the minimum magnitude legends explaining
magnitudes will show eight symbols in steps of one
magnitude.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B scheme.map.originSymbolScaleMag
Default: \fB4.9\fP
.sp
Type: \fIdouble\fP
.sp
Unit: \fIpx/magnitude\fP
.sp
The factor for scaling the symbol size of origins with
some magnitude as:
\(dqscheme.mag.originSymbolScaleMag\(dq * (magnitude \- \(dqscheme.mag.originSymbolMinMag\(dq).
.sp
The color of origins symbols is controlled by the parameters
\(dqscheme.colors.originSymbol.*\(dq.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B scheme.map.vectorLayerAntiAlias
Default: \fBfalse\fP
.sp
Type: \fIboolean\fP
.sp
Apply antialiasing to map layers.
This improves the visual quality but decreases performance.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B scheme.map.bilinearFilter
Default: \fBtrue\fP
.sp
Type: \fIboolean\fP
.sp
Apply bilinear filtering to maps.
The bilinear filter improves the visual quality but decreases
performance slightly. It is only used for static map images.
Not while dragging.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B scheme.map.showGrid
Default: \fBtrue\fP
.sp
Type: \fIboolean\fP
.sp
Display the latitude/longitude grid on maps
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B scheme.map.showCities
Default: \fBtrue\fP
.sp
Type: \fIboolean\fP
.sp
Show cities defined in \(dqcitiesXML\(dq on maps
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B scheme.map.cityPopulationWeight
Default: \fB150\fP
.sp
Type: \fIint\fP
.sp
Controls at which zoom level a city will be visible. The
following formula is used:
screen_width (km) * weight >= population
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B scheme.map.showLayers
Default: \fBtrue\fP
.sp
Type: \fIboolean\fP
.sp
Show custom layers on maps
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B scheme.map.showLegends
Default: \fBfalse\fP
.sp
Type: \fIboolean\fP
.sp
Show map legends initially. Some applications provide
controls to toggle the visibility in addition to this
option.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B scheme.map.projection
Default: \fBRectangular\fP
.sp
Type: \fIstring\fP
.sp
Values: \fBRectangular,Mercator\fP
.sp
The projection for showing maps. SeisComP ships with
Rectangular and Mercator.
Other projections may be provided through plugins.
.sp
The visible latitude range of maps shown with Mercator
is limited to \-85 \- +85 deg.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B scheme.map.toBGR
Default: \fBfalse\fP
.sp
Type: \fIboolean\fP
.sp
Converts map colors from RGB color scheme to BGR.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B scheme.map.polygonRoughness
Default: \fB3\fP
.sp
Type: \fIint\fP
.sp
Unit: \fIpx\fP
.sp
Minimum screen distance to plot a polygon or polyline line segment.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B scheme.map.maxZoom
Default: \fB24\fP
.sp
Type: \fIfloat\fP
.sp
Range: \fB1..24\fP
.sp
Maximum allowed zoom level.
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBscheme.colors.*\fP
\fIColors can be configured as rgb, rgba. hexadecimal numbers or color keyword names\fP
\fIdefined by W3C. If a color is unset, SeisComP applications\fP
\fIattempt to read it from your Desktop theme.\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B scheme.colors.background
Type: \fIcolor\fP
.sp
A general application background color. Can be used to give
each application a different background color. An unset value
lets Qt decide.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B scheme.colors.agencies
Type: \fIlist:string\-tuples\fP
.sp
Sets desired colors for particular agencyIDs. It depends on the
applications if they honor this setting or not. The event list
will render the agencyID string with the defined colors.
