.SS StdLoc extension
.sp
Generic locator plugin for SeisComP.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBStdLoc.*\fP
\fILocator parameters: StdLoc. This locator requires the plugin\fP
\fI\(dqstdloc\(dq to be loaded.\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B StdLoc.profiles
Type: \fIlist:string\fP
.sp
Defines a list of profiles to make available to the plugin.
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBStdLoc.profile.$name.*\fP
$name is a placeholder for the name to be used and needs to be added to \fI\%StdLoc.profiles\fP to become active.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
StdLoc.profiles = a,b
StdLoc.profile.a.value1 = ...
StdLoc.profile.b.value1 = ...
# c is not active because it has not been added
# to the list of StdLoc.profiles
StdLoc.profile.c.value1 = ...
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B StdLoc.profile.$name.method
Default: \fBLeastSquares\fP
.sp
Type: \fIstring\fP
.sp
Values: \fBLeastSquares,GridSearch,OctTree,GridSearch+LeastSquares,OctTree+LeastSquares\fP
.sp
The location method to use.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B StdLoc.profile.$name.tableType
Default: \fBLOCSAT\fP
.sp
Type: \fIstring\fP
.sp
Values: \fBhomogeneous,libtau,LOCSAT\fP
.sp
Type of travel\-time interface. Also consider
\(dqtableModel\(dq!
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B StdLoc.profile.$name.tableModel
Default: \fBiasp91\fP
.sp
Type: \fIstring\fP
.sp
The travel\-time model to be used. The
availability of models depends on
\(dqtableType\(dq.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B StdLoc.profile.$name.PSTableOnly
Default: \fBtrue\fP
.sp
Type: \fIboolean\fP
.sp
If enabled, the arrival travel time information are fetched
using \(aqP\(aq and \(aqS\(aq tables only and the user selected
specific phase type is not considered (e.g. Pg, Sg,
PmP, SmS, P1, S1, etc).
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B StdLoc.profile.$name.usePickUncertainties
Default: \fBfalse\fP
.sp
Type: \fIboolean\fP
.sp
Use pick time uncertainties rather than a fixed
time error of XXX s. If true, an arrival weight is
associated according to the uncertainty of the pick
and \(dqpickUncertaintyClasses\(dq.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B StdLoc.profile.$name.pickUncertaintyClasses
Default: \fB0.000,0.025,0.050,0.100,0.200,0.400\fP
.sp
Type: \fIlist:string\fP
.sp
Unit: \fIs\fP
.sp
Comma\-separated list of time limits of uncertainty
classes from which, along with pick time uncertainties,
arrival weights are computed. The first value
defines the lower limit of class 0.
.sp
The interval into which a pick time uncertainty falls
defines the index of the uncertainty class starting
with 0.
.sp
The corresponding arrival weight is computed as:
weight = 1 / 2^(index).
.sp
Example: A pick with a time uncertainty of 0.15 s is
within the 4th interval ranging from 0.1 to 0.2 s.
The class index is then 3.
.sp
If pick uncertainty is absent, the highest class index
applies.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B StdLoc.profile.$name.confLevel
Default: \fB0.9\fP
.sp
Type: \fIdouble\fP
.sp
Range: \fB0.5..1.0\fP
.sp
Confidence level, between 0.5 and 1.0, used in
computing the hypocenter confidence ellipsoid.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B StdLoc.profile.$name.enableConfidenceEllipsoid
Default: \fBfalse\fP
.sp
Type: \fIboolean\fP
.sp
Compute the hypocenter confidence ellipsoid. Disable
this optional parameter to save some computation time.
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBStdLoc.profile.$name.GridSearch.*\fP
\fIParameters controlling the GridSearch and OctTree methods.\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B StdLoc.profile.$name.GridSearch.center
Default: \fBauto,auto,20\fP
.sp
Type: \fIlist:string\fP
.sp
Unit: \fIdeg,deg,km\fP
.sp
Grid center defined as: latitude,longitude,depth. The
special value \(dqauto\(dq can be used and the corresponding latitude, longitude
and/or depth will be automatically computed as the average of the arrival
station locations.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B StdLoc.profile.$name.GridSearch.size
Default: \fB40,40,30\fP
.sp
Type: \fIlist:string\fP
.sp
Unit: \fIkm\fP
.sp
Grid size in km defined as: X,Y,Z
direction extents around the \(dqGridSearch.center\(dq,
where X is the longitudinal extent, Y the
latitudinal extent and Z the vertical extent.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B StdLoc.profile.$name.GridSearch.numPoints
Type: \fIlist:string\fP
.sp
Number of grid points in X, Y, Z
direction. The first and last points are on the
grid boundary unless the number of points is 1
and the point will be in the grid center.
.sp
Format: numX,numY,numZ.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B StdLoc.profile.$name.GridSearch.misfitType
Default: \fBL1\fP
.sp
Type: \fIstring\fP
.sp
Values: \fBL1,L2\fP
.sp
The type of misfit to use, from which
the likelihood function is derived: L1 or L2 norm.
L1 is less sensitive to outliers and so more
suitable with automatic picks, L2 is the preferred
choice for manual picks.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B StdLoc.profile.$name.GridSearch.travelTimeError
Default: \fB0.25\fP
.sp
Type: \fIdouble\fP
.sp
Unit: \fIs\fP
.sp
Typical error in seconds for travel times to
stations. The value affects the uncertainty
of the location. In OctTree it also influences
the probability density computation: too
conservative values increase the number of
iterations required by OctTree to converge
to a high resolution solution.
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBStdLoc.profile.$name.OctTree.*\fP
\fIParameters controlling the OctTree method. OctTree\fP
\fIuses the parameters defined in GridSearch, but\fP
\fIapplies the OctTree search algorithm on the grid.\fP
\fIThe starting cells of the OctTree search are created by\fP
\fIdividing the initial grid in equally sized cells.\fP
\fIThe grid points becomes the cell vertices.\fP
\fIResulting number of cells in each direction:\fP
\fI\(dqGridSearch.numPoints\(dq \- 1.\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B StdLoc.profile.$name.OctTree.maxIterations
Default: \fB50000\fP
.sp
Type: \fIint\fP
.sp
Maximum number of iterations after which the
search stops. Zero or negatives values disable
the stopping.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B StdLoc.profile.$name.OctTree.minCellSize
Default: \fB0.1\fP
.sp
Type: \fIdouble\fP
.sp
Unit: \fIkm\fP
.sp
Minimum cell size to be generate by the OctTree
search to stop. A zero or negative value disable
this stopping mechanism.
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBStdLoc.profile.$name.LeastSquares.*\fP
\fIParameters controlling the LeastSquares method.\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B StdLoc.profile.$name.LeastSquares.depthInit
Default: \fB20\fP
.sp
Type: \fIdouble\fP
.sp
The initial depth estimate when no initial
hypocenter is provided. Used only with
\(aqLeastSquares\(aq.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B StdLoc.profile.$name.LeastSquares.iterations
Default: \fB20\fP
.sp
Type: \fIint\fP
.sp
Number of iterations. Each iteration will
use the location and time from the previous
Least Squares solution.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B StdLoc.profile.$name.LeastSquares.dampingFactor
Default: \fB0.0\fP
.sp
Type: \fIdouble\fP
.sp
Damping factor to be used when solving the
system of equations.
.sp
0: no damping.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B StdLoc.profile.$name.LeastSquares.solverType
Default: \fBLSMR\fP
.sp
Type: \fIstring\fP
.sp
Values: \fBLSMR,LSQR\fP
.sp
Algorithm to use: either LSMR or LSQR.
.UNINDENT
